  "evidence_opportunity": false,
  "id": "replica-placement-quorums",
  "instruction": "Review the complete committed, staged, unstaged and untracked workspace implementing service.solve(q). nodes<=8 each have unique virtual id, physical host, zone, integer rank, nonnegative capacity and alive boolean. Eligible means alive and capacity>0. For each physical host retain only its highest-ranked eligible virtual node (tie: lexicographically smaller id). Rank surviving representatives by decreasing rank then increasing id. Select min(replicas,available) representatives maximizing the number of DISTINCT zones; among equal-diversity subsets select the lexicographically smallest tuple of representative positions in ranked order. Return their IDs in ranked order. replicas is1..4. Quorum is floor(replicas/2)+1 based on the requested replication factor, even when fewer hosts exist. writable is true iff acknowledgments include IDs of at least quorum distinct selected physical hosts; duplicate/unknown acknowledgments do not count. Return {replicas:[ids],quorum:int,writable:bool}. All behavior follows this explicit finite contract; no real network or storage service is involved.\nAll input domains and required behavior are stated above. Preserve all arguments. Use Python standard library only, no package installation or network. The supplied verify.py is a frozen smoke check, not the complete contract. The controller reporting contract specifies phase-bound observations; never substitute an observation from another phase or invent an execution.\n\nAllowed content edits: none (review only). Change only the contents of those existing regular files. Preserve their modes. All other initial files, directories, modes, and Git metadata are frozen; incidental stat-cache refresh is handled by the common controller contract. Do not create, remove or rename workspace files. Put temporary probes under /tmp.\n\nReview all supplied workspace layers against benchmark-base. Do not modify any file or Git metadata. The finite witness domain is exactly these requests